---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageMeta from '@/components/PageMeta.astro';
import AuthorityPanel from '@/components/ia/AuthorityPanel.astro';
import GatewayCard from '@/components/ia/GatewayCard.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="SPDTF 2.0 Development"
  description="The SPDTF 2.0 development workspace: evidence-up modelling, bounded contexts, working groups and reviewable candidates."
>
  <PageMeta category="SPDTF 2.0 Development" variant="brand" updated="In development · 2026-08-18" />
  <h1>SPDTF 2.0 Development</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    SPDTF 2.0 is the current development generation of the Smart Property Data Trust
    Framework. It is a domain-led, evidence-up process for making meaning reviewable;
    it is not an adopted standard, approved model or replacement implementation.
  </p>

  <AuthorityPanel destination="spdtf-2" />

  <div class="callout callout--key">
    <p class="callout__label">Development status</p>
    <p>
      Human working groups own domain meaning. Governance controls later promotion. AI
      can extract, compare and draft, but it receives no standards authority. A machine
      validation result proves only the encoded checks, not semantic agreement.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="method">Evidence-up modelling</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Agree scope, users, exclusions and competency questions.</li>
    <li>Collect participant language, rules, examples, documents and recognised sources with appropriate handling controls.</li>
    <li>Draft context-owned semantic outputs and an ontology candidate from the evidence.</li>
    <li>Check provenance, coverage, constraints and conformance; publish open questions.</li>
    <li>Review, revise and record dispositions before any governed release.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    The existing <a href="/v2">Property Pack seed</a> is a structured SPDTF 2.0
    development input: machine-generated, non-normative, and not reviewed or approved
    by a working group. Its stable <code>/v2/**</code> routes remain retained inputs.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ontology-journey">Ontologies and semantic modelling</h2>
  <p>
    This journey starts with business questions and keeps semantic meaning distinct from
    validation, projections, implementation and governance. Each page uses the same
    authority contract and links the next reviewable step.
  </p>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf-2/ontologies/why-ontologies" title="Why ontologies" description="What an ontology adds beyond a document schema, in business language." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf-2/ontologies/semantic-package" title="Six-part semantic package" description="Glossary, dictionary, taxonomies, controlled vocabularies, resources and relationships." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf-2/ontologies/bounded-contexts" title="Bounded contexts and common boundary" description="Keep local precision while making cross-context exchange explicit." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf-2/ontologies/coverage" title="Coverage crosswalk" description="The separate four-lens, 11-theme workshop view and eight formal concerns." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf-2/ontologies/standards" title="Standards, vocabularies and frameworks" description="Targets, candidates and references with bounded conformance and status claims." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf-2/ontologies/evidence-and-mappings" title="Evidence, provenance and mappings" description="Trace claims and distinguish all five mapping meanings." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf-2/ontologies/validation" title="Validation and generated projections" description="Conformance, lifecycle, receipts and tested downstream representations." />
  </div>

  <h2 id="workspace">Development workspace</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf-2/working-groups" title="Working groups" eyebrow="Canonical workspace" description="The seven named groups plus the peer Interoperability Working Group." />
    <GatewayCard href="/v2" title="Development input: Property Pack seed" eyebrow="Retained input" description="Explore the structured machine-generated pre-draft, with its non-normative status." />
    <GatewayCard href="/governance" title="Governance" eyebrow="Shared service" description="Decision rights, status, lifecycle and promotion records live in one authority tree." />
  </div>
</Layout>
